Revision: 9948ff97e99919ead98df10aa76b68dc956d8959 (plan 6f2e91f), on top of W19 2b3944a.
Changed in stage-4/ since 2b3944a (builder paths only):
  - New: src/handlers/batches.ts; test/w20-batches.test.ts.
  - Changed: src/state.ts, history.ts, routes.ts, snapshot.ts (one line: imported revisions carry no batch id until W21), handlers/corrections.ts.
What it does, by plan section:
  1. State: a revision carries its batch id (null unless a batch recorded it). Each settlement id indexes its members: the payments that carry it, whether made by the API, seeded or imported (D98).
  2. Revision view (D97): `correction_batch_id` only on a revision a batch recorded, in the batch response, its replays and GET /payments/{id}/revisions. Every other revision keeps stage 3's six fields, and statement entries are unchanged.
  3. History check (3.8, I58): takes any number of proposed revisions together. A single correction passes one; a batch passes all of its own.
  4. POST /correction-batches (3.9 steps 1-14, D95-D100), the tenth idempotent path:
